s-reports-list/">http://www.who.int/tdr/svc/publications/about-tdr/progress-reports-list/</ext-link>. Geneva: WHO/TDR. Accessed 30 October 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000307-TDR8"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>TDR</collab><year>2008</year><article-title>TropIKA web site.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.tropika.net/">http://www.tropika.net/</ext-link>. Accessed 30 October 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000307-WHO1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>WHO</collab><year>2008</year><article-title>Global strategy and plan of action on public health, innovation and intellectual property.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/phi">http://www.who.int/phi</ext-link>. Accessed 30 October 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000307-Hopkins1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hopkins</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Witty</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Nwaka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Mission possible.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>449</volume><fpage>166</fpage><lpage>169</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17851512</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000307-TDR9"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>TDR</collab><year>2008</year><source>Community-directed interventions for major health problems in Africa: a multi-country study</source><publisher-loc>Geneva</publisher-loc><publisher-name>WHO/TDR</publisher-name><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/tdr/svc/publications/tdr-research-publications/community-directed-interventions-health-problems">http://www.who.int/tdr/svc/publications/tdr-research-publications/community-directed-interventions-health-problems</ext-link>. Accessed 30 October 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000307-The1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>The Global Fund and TDR</collab><year>2008</year><source>Framework for operations and implementation research in health and disease control programmes</source><publisher-loc>Geneva</publisher-loc><publisher-name>The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria and TDR</publisher-name><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.theglobalfund.org/documents/me/FrameworkForOperationsResearch.pdf">http://www.theglobalfund.org/documents/me/FrameworkForOperationsResearch.pdf</ext-link>. Accessed 30 October 2008</comment></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p>Robert Ridley has been Director of TDR since June 2004. Peter Ndumbe has been a member of TDR's Scientific and Technical Advisory Committee since 2004 and has been chair of the committee since 2005, and Rolf Korte was vice-chair of TDR's Joint Coordinating Board in 2006 and has been chair since 2007. Neither Peter Ndumbe nor Rolf Korte are in receipt of research funds from TDR, nor do they receive any remuneration, other than expenses, for their contribution to TDR.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p>The authors received no specific funding to write this article.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>